    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0464" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/113.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister to the
                        Dominican Republic</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[After repeating the telegram from Mr. Furniss, dated June 6, the telegram
                    continues:]</p>
                <p>If this is true, you will at once impress upon the Dominican Government the
                    necessity for refraining from any such action.</p>
                <pb facs="0465" n="349" xml:id="pg349"/>
                <p>The boundary dispute negotiations have been held up for more than a month by
                    Peynado’s delay in presenting a memorandum promised to the Department regarding
                    encroachments by Haiti on Dominican territory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
